  "description": "I fluttered a plastic spatula in front of my TLM-103 in the studio. It's recorded at 96K, 32 bits, so you can stretch it or pitch it any way you want. If you want it to sound small you'll want to filter off the low end. On the other hand, you can probably get some fun gigantic effects by using just the bass, or even pitching it down.\n\nThis was for the moth wing flutter in \"Molly Moth Saves Christmas\":\n<a href=\"http://kidpodtheater.com/molly-moth-saves-christmas/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://kidpodtheater.com/molly-moth-saves-christmas/</a>",
